-- title:
--   Unique algebra equivalence from an exact polynomial evaluation kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $A$ be a commutative $R$-algebra, and let $x\in A$. Suppose that $m\in R[T]$ describes the exact polynomial evaluation kernel:
--   $$
--   q(x)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad m\mid q
--   \qquad(q\in R[T]).
--   $$
--   Evaluation uses the specified $R$-algebra structure. Write $R[x]\subseteq A$ for the subalgebra generated by $x$ and $(m)$ for the principal ideal of $R[T]$ generated by $m$.
--
--   There exists a unique $R$-algebra isomorphism
--   $$
--   e:R[T]/(m)\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}R[x]
--   $$
--   such that, after including $R[x]$ into $A$,
--   $$
--   e([q])=q(x)\qquad(q\in R[T]).
--   $$
--   Uniqueness is among isomorphisms satisfying this evaluation formula. In particular, the polynomial class $[T]$ maps to $x$.
--
--   No field, monicity, finite-dimensionality or nontriviality assumption is required. The coefficient ring may have zero divisors, and the polynomial $m$ may be zero. The codomain is the generated subalgebra $R[x]$.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission. At Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq and its quotient-representative formula are in RingTheory/Ideal/Quotient/Operations.lean lines 766-773; Ideal.quotientKerEquivRange is in lines 808-813; Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval is in RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.lean lines 52-54. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Ideal/Quotient/Operations.html#Ideal.quotientKerEquivRange and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.html#Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval . An exact divisibility description of polynomial evaluation yields a unique R-algebra equivalence R[T]/(m) to R[x] carrying the class of q to q(x). The proof is the first isomorphism theorem followed by the identification of the evaluation image with the generated subalgebra; uniqueness follows from quotient representatives. Coefficients and target are arbitrary commutative rings with a specified algebra structure. No monicity, field, finite-dimensionality or nontriviality assumption; no platform theorem dependencies or new definitions.

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Polynomial.Basic

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.evaluation_kernel_adjoin_equivalence
    (R A : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    (x : A) (m : Polynomial R)
    (hker : ∀ q : Polynomial R, q.eval₂ (algebraMap R A) x = 0 ↔ m ∣ q) :
    ∃! e : (Polynomial R ⧸ Ideal.span ({m} : Set (Polynomial R))) ≃ₐ[R]
        Algebra.adjoin R ({x} : Set A),
      ∀ q : Polynomial R,
        (e (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {m}) q) : A) =
          q.eval₂ (algebraMap R A) x := by sorry
